<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#AnalogicalMapping> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#promptExtractionText> "Extract Metaphorical and Analogical Mapping elements from the image. Metaphorical and Analogical Mapping includes: symbolic representations, analogical elements, metaphorical connections, symbolic mappings, figurative elements, and analogical relationships. For each metaphorical element found, provide: 1) A descriptive instance_name (e.g., 'fire_metaphor', 'smile_analogy'), 2) A natural language label (e.g., 'the fire metaphor', 'the smile analogy'), 3) A brief description of the metaphorical or analogical meaning. Focus on how one element represents or symbolizes another concept. Example output format: {\"instance_name\": \"fire_metaphor\", \"label\": \"the fire metaphor\", \"description\": \"The burning house serves as a metaphor for chaos or destruction, contrasting with the girl's calm expression\"}"@en .
_:n742c0716f0154719a847bf96a95b6370b68 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:n742c0716f0154719a847bf96a95b6370b69 .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#horizontallyAdjacentTo> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#objectEmbeddedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Indicates text naturally appearing on clothing, objects, and surfaces within meme scenes"@en .
_:n742c0716f0154719a847bf96a95b6370b95 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:n742c0716f0154719a847bf96a95b6370b96 .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#perspectivallyContradicting> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Indicates two dimensions offering different viewpoints on another dimension in memes, e.g. same visual content from different perspectives"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiTransparentOverlaidOn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> _:n742c0716f0154719a847bf96a95b6370b97 .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01469#mapping_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The text 'when you punch the muslim kid so hard that he starts having seizures and fucking dies' is juxtaposed with the visual of a heavily armed soldier. The text implies that this violent act is equivalent to defusing a bomb, which is then explicitly stated in the second text chunk 'the bomb has been defused'. The soldier, as a visual entity associated with authority, danger, and heroism in combat scenarios, is mapped onto the act of 'defusing' the 'bomb' (i.e., the Muslim child). This creates an analogical mapping where the soldier's role is projected onto the violent act described in the text, framing it as a necessary or heroic action."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dramaticallyIronicalTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Indicates one dimension revealing information another dimension does not provide in memes, e.g. text revealing information visuals don't show"@en .
_:n742c0716f0154719a847bf96a95b6370b32 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:n742c0716f0154719a847bf96a95b6370b33 .
